<title>USA: Gentex says GM strike impact minimal.</title>
<headline>Gentex says GM strike impact minimal.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gentex Corp said the impact on its operations of the General Motors Corp strike in Canada has been minimal.</p>
<p>&quot;It's had minimal effect at this point,&quot; said Gentex spokeswoman Connie Hamblin.</p>
<p>Mesirow Financial analyst Greg Salchow estimated in a report on Monday that &quot;a strike that fully idles GM's production would cost Gentex about $0.02 to $0.03 per week.&quot;</p>
<p>Salchow projects that Gentex will earn $0.22 per share in the fourth quarter and $0.77 per share for 1996, excluding a $4 million litigation settlement charge.</p>
<p>He said his 1996 estimate excludes possible strike impact.</p>
<p>Regarding Salchow's strike impact estimate, Hamblin said, &quot;Given what I know, I think that's a high estimate. A lot of it depends on the depth and the duration of the strike.&quot;</p>
<p>Shares in the Zeeland, Mich.-based manufacturer of automatic dimming rearview mirrors and fire protection products were up 1/4 to 25-1/4.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
